  NZ: {"independence":"26 September 1907 (from the UK)","dependentAreas":"Tokelau (1)","constitution":"New Zealand has no single constitution document; the Constitution Act 1986, effective 1 January 1987, includes only part of the uncodified constitution; others include a collection of statutes or \"acts of Parliament,\" the Treaty of Waitangi, Orders in Council, letters patent, court decisions, and unwritten conventions","amendment":"proposed as bill by Parliament or by referendum called either by the government or by citizens; passage of a bill as an act normally requires two separate readings with committee reviews in between to make changes and corrections, a third reading approved by the House of Representatives membership or by the majority of votes in a referendum, and assent of the governor-general; passage of amendments to reserved constitutional provisions affecting the term of Parliament, electoral districts, and voting restrictions…","internationalLaw":"accepts compulsory ICJ jurisdiction with reservations; accepts ICCt jurisdiction","citizenship":{"birth":"no","descent":"at least one parent must be a citizen of New Zealand","dual":"yes","residency":"3 years"},"organisations":65,"un":true,"deployments":"small numbers of NZ military personnel are deployed on a variety of international missions in Africa, Antarctica, the Asia-Pacific region, and the Middle East (2025)","holiday":"Waitangi Day, 6 February (1840); Anzac Day, 25 April (1915)"},
